# Supabase project credentials (Project Settings → API).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Optional: server-only key for privileged operations (seed script, admin
# tasks). Never expose this to the browser.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# GitHub and LinkedIn sign-in are enabled per-project in the Supabase
# dashboard (Authentication → Providers), not read from this app's env —
# the client ID/secret you create with each provider go in *there*, not
# here. Listed below only as a reference for what to create:
#   GitHub:   github.com/settings/developers → OAuth App
#             callback URL: <your-supabase-url>/auth/v1/callback
#             Request the "public_repo" scope when connecting (Settings →
#             Integrations does this automatically) to enable the
#             Dashboard's GitHub Commits card and synced repo list — the
#             OAuth token itself is captured and encrypted by this app
#             (github_connections.access_token_encrypted), same
#             AES-256-GCM/TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY as the Google connection
#             below.
#   LinkedIn: linkedin.com/developers → Create app, request "Sign In with
#             LinkedIn using OpenID Connect", same callback URL pattern.
#             This only ever grants name/email/photo — LinkedIn doesn't
#             expose job listings, connections, or messages to apps
#             outside its restricted partner program.

# --- Career Agent ------------------------------------------------------
# None of the below are required for Career Profile, Job Search, Job
# Match, Applications, Interviews, Assessments, Career Analytics,
# LinkedIn sign-in, GitHub sync, or live job search (Arbeitnow, keyless)
# — those all work already. Unset, the remaining Career Hub features show
# an explicit "Connection Required" state rather than pretending to be
# connected. See ARCHITECTURE.md → "Career Agent" for what each unlocks.

# AI provider key — powers AI resume tailoring and cover letter
# generation (both built; try them from a job's detail page). Also
# required for the Career Inbox's email classification/drafting once
# Gmail is connected below. The deterministic Job Match score does not
# need this — it works without any AI provider.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Google OAuth app for Gmail + Calendar (Career Inbox, interview
# scheduling). UNLIKE the GitHub/LinkedIn entries above, this one IS read
# directly by the app (lib/google/oauth.ts) — it's a custom OAuth flow,
# not Supabase's identity linking, because it needs offline access (a
# refresh token) and specific Gmail/Calendar scopes that Supabase's
# generic Google sign-in doesn't request.
#   1. console.cloud.google.com → new/existing project
#   2. APIs & Services → Library → enable Gmail API + Google Calendar API
#   3. APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen → External → add scopes
#      gmail.readonly, gmail.compose, calendar.events → add yourself as a
#      test user
#   4. APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth client ID → Web application
#      → authorized redirect URI: <your-app-url>/auth/google/callback
#      (and http://localhost:3000/auth/google/callback for local dev)
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Required alongside the above — encrypts the Google refresh token at
# rest (AES-256-GCM; see lib/crypto/token-encryption.ts). Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# Losing/rotating this invalidates every stored Google connection (users
# just reconnect). Never reuse this value for anything else.
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Optional: an additional job board/aggregator API for more live-search
# coverage than the built-in keyless source (Arbeitnow) provides — e.g.
# Adzuna, Jooble, or USAJobs. Pick one whose terms permit this use.
JOB_BOARD_API_KEY=

# --- Business module (Team/Agency CRM + simplified ERP) ----------------
# No env vars needed — nothing here. Organizations, CRM, invoicing,
# purchase orders, payroll, and reports (/business/*) run entirely on the
# Supabase credentials above; there's no external provider to connect.
# See ARCHITECTURE.md → "Business Module" for the org/RLS model and what's
# deliberately out of scope (real payment/payroll processing, formal
# accounting).
